comments.body:
@julianoes Yes, I tried and it works if I put the "export" keyword. 

My fault, maybe I misspelled the variable name when I tried the first time and, moreover, I didn't remember well the "export" effect: the application I run is not anymore the shell process, thus without "export" the variable will go out of scope. Thus, it is a viable solution to the problem, and including the variable in the .bashrc it will avoid me adding it every bash session.

Thanks

